---One tool with its effective policy for the requested scope.
---@class posthog.mcp_gateway.ResolvedToolPolicy
---@field tool_name string Tool name as exposed by the upstream server.
---@field description string Tool description from the upstream server.
---@field input_schema posthog.mcp_gateway.ResolvedToolPolicyInputSchemaMap JSON Schema describing the tool's input arguments.
---@field is_destructive boolean Whether the canonical gateway heuristic treats this tool as destructive.
---@field is_read_only boolean Whether the tool only reads data: the server marks it readOnlyHint and its name starts with a read verb and has no write or destructive verb.
---@field policy_state posthog.mcp_gateway.MCPToolApprovalStateEnum Effective state for the scope. * `approved` - Approved * `needs_approval` - Needs approval * `do_not_use` - Do not use
---@field team_state posthog.mcp_gateway.MCPToolApprovalStateEnum|distilled.Null What the team-level chain (row or preset) yields, ignoring the scope. Null when the team imposes nothing. * `approved` - Approved * `needs_approval` - Needs approval * `do_not_use` - Do not use
---@field locked boolean True when no state is editable for this scope (a rule match or a Blocked team ceiling).
---@field decided_by posthog.mcp_gateway.DecidedByEnum Which policy layer decided the state. * `rule` - rule * `scope` - scope * `team` - team * `preset` - preset * `legacy` - legacy * `default` - default
---@field rule_name string Matching org rule name, when decided_by is rule.
---@field rule_description string Matching org rule description, when decided_by is rule.

